.TH S3AR-LIST 1 "September 2026" "S3 Archiver" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3ar-list \- list live S3 buckets and objects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3ar-list
.RB [ \-v ]
.I s3://[BUCKET[/KEY]]...
.br
.B s3ar-list
.B \-b
.RB [ \-v ]
.B s3://
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s3ar-list
lists live S3 objects selected by one or more S3 URIs. The URI
.B s3://
selects all buckets and their objects. A bucket URI selects that bucket and
its objects; a key URI selects the exact key and keys below KEY/.
Matches stop at path boundaries, and a trailing slash does not change the
selection. See
.BR s3ar (1)
for selection examples.
.PP
Bucket and key names in operands are literal, not URL-decoded. Quote operands
containing spaces or shell metacharacters. Operands are processed in order;
overlapping selections produce repeated output. A key selection that matches
neither an object nor descendants is an error. Empty buckets are valid.
.PP
With
.BR \-b ,
list bucket names only. This mode requires exactly
.BR s3:// .
.PP
Listing results are written to standard output; diagnostics go to standard
error. Bucket names are printed before their selected objects, including for
key selections. Names have the
.B s3://
prefix and use the byte-oriented URL encoding described in
.BR s3ar (1).
.PP
With
.BR \-v ,
object rows have this form:
.PP
.nf
s3://BUCKET/KEY size=BYTES mtime=SECONDS etag=ETAG
.fi
.PP
Modification time is in seconds since the Unix epoch; an unavailable ETag
is printed as
.BR \- .
With
.BR \-bv ,
bucket rows have the form
.BR "s3://BUCKET acl=SUMMARY" .
ACLs are fetched only in bucket-only mode with
.BR \-v .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b , " " \-\-buckets
List buckets only.
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-\-verbose
Include object size, modification time, and ETag; with
.BR \-b ,
include bucket ACL information instead. One occurrence also enables info
diagnostics, two enable debug, and three enable HTTP trace. Further
occurrences have no effect.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Display command usage on standard error and exit successfully.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Increase diagnostic verbosity by one level, up to trace.
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Decrease diagnostic verbosity by one level, down to fatal.
.PP
These signals do not change the listing fields selected by
.BR \-v .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR S3AR_ENDPOINT ,
.BR S3AR_REGION ,
.BR S3AR_URI_STYLE ,
.BR S3AR_ACCESS_KEY ,
.BR S3AR_SECRET_KEY ,
and
.B S3AR_SESSION_TOKEN
configure the S3 connection in the same way as for
.BR s3ar (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing or help completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
S3 client initialization or standard-output flush failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage, invalid configuration, allocation failure, or an S3 operation
failed.
.PP
When an S3 operation fails after a retry, the diagnostic includes the number
of attempts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3ar (1),
.BR s3ar-delete (1),
.BR s3ar-get (1),
.BR s3ar-put (1)
